        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-content">
            <p>Biomimetic dentistry mimics nature by preserving and restoring teeth using materials and techniques that work with your tooth's natural structure, not against it. This approach avoids crowns and root canals by addressing decay conservatively while strengthening your teeth.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          How is this different from traditional dentistry?
          <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-content">
            <p>Traditional dentistry removes large amounts of healthy tooth structure to place crowns. Biomimetic dentistry preserves maximum tooth structure using advanced bonding techniques and biocompatible materials that actually strengthen your teeth.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Does Dr. Noot really never place crowns?
          <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
